# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the WDC Learning Portal client application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Updated `package-lock.json` with new dependency tree

### 2. Component Integration
Modified `client/src/App.jsx`:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component next to the existing `<Analytics />` component in the main App export
- Placement follows the official Vercel documentation for React applications

### 3. Files Modified
- `client/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `client/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies
- `client/src/App.jsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component

## Implementation Details

The SpeedInsights component was placed at the root level of the application, inside the AuthProvider wrapper alongside the existing Analytics component. This ensures that Speed Insights tracking is active across all pages of the application.

The implementation follows the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart documentation for React applications:
- Component is imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- No additional configuration required
- Works seamlessly with the existing Vite + React setup

## Verification

✓ Build completed successfully with no errors
✓ All dependencies installed correctly
✓ Build artifacts (dist/) properly excluded from git
✓ Package lock file updated appropriately
✓ Code follows existing patterns (matching Analytics component integration)

## Next Steps

After deploying to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance data
2. Metrics can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section
3. The tracking script will be injected at runtime when deployed on Vercel
4. Consider upgrading to Speed Insights Plus for enhanced features if needed

## Notes

- This project is a Vite + React application
- The codebase already had Vercel Analytics configured, making this integration straightforward
- No linter or test suite was available to run, but the build completed successfully
- The SpeedInsights component is lightweight and has no visible UI impact
